WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.383 --> 00:00:07.903
In the mouse cortex, radial glia make neurons first, then astrocytes.

2
00:00:08.643 --> 00:00:10.163
Same progenitors, new output.

3
00:00:11.123 --> 00:00:12.123
What changes?

4
00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:17.300
In rodent cortex, the best-studied route to astrocytes uses cytokines.

5
00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:20.180
Its evidence sorts into three conditions.

6
00:00:21.283 --> 00:00:23.723
First, a progenitor must still be there.

7
00:00:24.543 --> 00:00:27.463
Proneural genes push dividing cells to become neurons.

8
00:00:28.533 --> 00:00:33.913
Notch turns on Hes repressors, which hold proneural genes down, so the cell stays a

9
00:00:33.913 --> 00:00:34.913
progenitor.

10
00:00:35.383 --> 00:00:37.663
Notch does not make astrocytes by itself.

11
00:00:38.563 --> 00:00:40.563
It keeps a reserve of progenitors for later.

12
00:00:41.633 --> 00:00:43.473
Second, the signal must arrive.

13
00:00:44.333 --> 00:00:49.333
It is a family of cytokines: CNTF, LIF and cardiotrophin-1.

14
00:00:50.333 --> 00:00:55.473
Their shared receptor subunit, gp130, activates JAK kinases.

15
00:00:56.583 --> 00:00:58.663
JAK phosphorylates STAT3.

16
00:00:59.483 --> 00:01:03.183
STAT3 switches on astrocyte genes, such as GFAP.

17
00:01:04.233 --> 00:01:07.233
Third, the progenitor must be able to read the signal.

18
00:01:08.013 --> 00:01:09.013
That is competence.

19
00:01:10.033 --> 00:01:14.333
Give CNTF to cortical progenitors early in neurogenesis.

20
00:01:15.193 --> 00:01:18.073
They have the receptor, and STAT3 can be activated.

21
00:01:19.013 --> 00:01:20.013
What happens?

22
00:01:26.067 --> 00:01:29.047
Few GFAP-positive astrocytes appear.

23
00:01:29.967 --> 00:01:34.847
In these early cells, the STAT3 site in the GFAP promoter is methylated.

24
00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:39.380
A methyl group on that site keeps STAT3 from binding there.

25
00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:43.820
STAT3 is active, but the GFAP gene does not answer.

26
00:01:44.833 --> 00:01:49.773
Later, demethylation and other changes in the cell let the same cytokine switch on

27
00:01:49.773 --> 00:01:50.773
GFAP.

28
00:01:54.867 --> 00:01:59.767
So gliogenesis is timed partly inside the cell, not only by when the signal shows

29
00:01:59.767 --> 00:02:00.767
up.

30
00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:06.160
What unlocks it? Cells that have just committed to becoming neurons carry Notch

31
00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:07.160
ligands.

32
00:02:07.583 --> 00:02:12.163
In mouse cortex, Notch signaling in neighbouring progenitors induces a transcription

33
00:02:12.163 --> 00:02:14.023
factor, NFIA.

34
00:02:15.233 --> 00:02:17.853
NFIA helps remove the methyl groups.

35
00:02:18.753 --> 00:02:22.933
So Notch, which first held progenitors back, has a second job: competence.

36
00:02:23.833 --> 00:02:28.673
So, on this cortical cytokine route, a progenitor makes astrocytes when it is still

37
00:02:28.673 --> 00:02:31.333
there, given the signal, and able to read it.
